⨯ union-key: union discriminator for 'CharUnion' cannot be @optional
  @ test.idl:2:25

 2 │ union CharUnion switch(@optional char) {
   │                         ˆˆˆˆˆˆˆˆ @optional not allowed on discriminator
 3 │ case 'a':
 4 │     @key string a_value;

  ? remove @optional from the discriminator
  * union discriminators must always be present

⨯ union-key: union variant 'a_value' cannot use @key
  @ test.idl:4:6

 2 │ union CharUnion switch(@optional char) {
 3 │ case 'a':
 4 │     @key string a_value;
   │      ˆˆˆ @key not allowed on union variant
 5 │ case 'b':
 6 │     string b_value;

  ? remove @key from the variant or move it to the discriminator
  * only the union discriminator can be marked as @key

! char-discriminator: char types should not be used as union discriminators
  @ test.idl:2:34

 2 │ union CharUnion switch(@optional char) {
   │                                  ˆˆˆˆ char type
 3 │ case 'a':
 4 │     @key string a_value;

  ? consider using an integer or enum value instead
